BicDB is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, subject to the following
additional conditions. Together, these conditions and the verbatim Apache text
below are the BicDB License: source-available, not unmodified Apache-2.0 or an
OSI-approved open-source license. See LICENSE-SCOPE.md for covered code and licensors.

1. Managed database service
   Without a separate written commercial license from an authorized BicDB licensor,
   you may not offer BicDB or a derivative as a general-purpose hosted or managed
   database service to third parties for workloads they choose. This includes free
   tiers, dedicated instances, per-customer containers, customer-cloud offerings,
   and access through SQL, REST, MCP, SDKs or proxies. Application-specific search,
   reporting, imports and business APIs do not themselves make an application a
   general-purpose database service. Customer-directed consulting or administration
   of the customer's own deployment is allowed; an independently supplied managed
   database offering is not exempt merely because it runs in the customer's account.

2. Database product / OEM
   Without that commercial license, you may not sell, commercially license, OEM,
   white-label or otherwise commercially distribute BicDB or a derivative primarily
   as a standalone database engine, appliance or platform. Renaming, a protocol
   adapter, an agent interface or a thin wrapper does not change that boundary.
   Substantive applications with embedded or bundled supporting BicDB storage,
   consulting and support subscriptions, and ordinary community forks, patches,
   builds, mirrors and package registries are allowed. Incidental download, storage
   or physical-media charges are not database-product sales.

3. BicDB console branding
   Without that commercial license, when redistributing BicDB's own included
   administration console you may not remove or replace its BicDB origin attribution
   for a white-label database offering. Accessibility, translation, styling and
   layout changes are allowed if attribution remains clear. Forks may use another
   name while retaining BicDB origin attribution and avoiding implied endorsement.
   Independent applications need no BicDB logo or powered-by badge; an unused
   console need not be recreated. Third-party credits remain separately required.

The boundary is what the recipient is supplied: an application that uses a database,
or a database product/service. Personal, educational, nonprofit, internal production
and commercial application use are allowed, including proprietary applications and
SaaS of any size. There are no revenue, employee, tenant, user or instance limits.
Private modifications need not be published. Constrained sample-data demonstrations
and temporary evaluations are allowed; ongoing arbitrary third-party database
hosting falls under exception 1, even if free.

All grants below for covered BicDB rights are subject to these three conditions,
which prevail on conflict. References to "this License" below mean this complete
document, including for section 4's license-copy requirement. You may license your
own modifications under different terms as section 4 permits; those terms cannot
grant reserved rights to underlying BicDB code. No rights are granted on behalf
of a rights holder without its authorization. Previously granted rights and
separate third-party licenses are unchanged. A separate commercial
agreement overrides these conditions only within its stated scope. Later license
versions do not automatically change the terms of copies already received.

Except for these additional conditions and their application above, the Apache
License 2.0 applies without alteration. Its text follows verbatim.

